      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0071",
      "sequence": 926,
      "meaning": "Knowing the gods to be afraid, the treasury of compassion draws his bow to his ear and fills Kumbhakarṇa’s mouth with arrows. Still the giant charges like embodied Death. Rāma severs his head, which falls before Rāvaṇa, and then splits the onrushing torso in two. Its fall crushes monkeys, bears and demons, while Kumbhakarṇa’s radiance merges into the Lord’s face. The gods rejoice, praise Rāma and depart; Nārada arrives, sings the Lord’s virtues in a beautiful heroic strain, urges him to kill the wicked quickly, and leaves Rāma resplendent on the battlefield.",
