      "meaning": "At day’s end both armies withdraw, exhausted from battle. Rāma’s grace has increased the monkeys’ strength like fire fed with dry grass, while demons dwindle day and night like merit proclaimed by one’s own mouth. Rāvaṇa laments over his brother’s head. Meghanāda consoles him and promises to display the power and chariot received from his chosen deity. At dawn monkeys and demons clash at all four gates; then Meghanāda mounts his enchanted chariot, rises into the sky, and terrifies the monkey host with a thunderous laugh.",
