    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0073",
      "sequence": 928,
      "meaning": "Hidden in the sky, Meghanāda rains spears, swords, axes, clubs, stones and countless arrows until every direction is covered. No one can see who strikes. The monkeys leap upward with mountains and trees but return wounded; by illusion he makes every difficult pass and cave an arrow-cage. He disables Hanumān, Aṅgada, Nala, Nīla, Lakṣmaṇa, Sugrīva and Vibhīṣaṇa, then fights Rāma. His arrows become serpents and bind the Lord in a serpent-noose. Rāma, eternally free and sovereign, accepts the bonds as an actor’s play to beautify the battle; Śiva asks how the all-pervading abode of the universe, whose name releases sages from worldly bonds, could truly be bound.",
