    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0074",
      "sequence": 929,
      "meaning": "Śiva tells Pārvatī that Rāma’s embodied deeds cannot be measured by logic, speech or intellectual power; discerning renunciants therefore relinquish argument and worship him. Meghanāda has routed the army and reappears to boast, but Jāmbavān challenges him. The demon hurls a trident; Jāmbavān catches it, strikes him in the chest, whirls him by the feet and flings him into Laṅkā. Because a boon prevents his death, he survives. Nārada sends Garuḍa, who swiftly reaches Rāma and devours the illusory serpents. Freed of the spell, the monkey companies rejoice and angrily storm the fortress as the demons flee.",
