    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0075",
      "sequence": 930,
      "meaning": "Recovering from his swoon and ashamed before his father, Meghanāda retires to a mountain cave to perform an invincibility sacrifice. Vibhīṣaṇa warns Rāma that if the impure rite succeeds the tormentor of the gods will be unconquerable. Rāma sends Lakṣmaṇa with Aṅgada, Nīla, Mainda, Nala and Hanumān to destroy the rite and kill him, while Jāmbavān, Sugrīva and Vibhīṣaṇa guard the army. Armed with bow and quiver and sustained by Rāma’s majesty, Lakṣmaṇa vows not to return without slaying Meghanāda, even should a hundred Śivas aid him.",
