      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0076",
      "sequence": 931,
      "meaning": "The monkeys find Meghanāda seated at the rite, offering blood and buffaloes. They wreck the sacrifice, pull his hair and kick him when he refuses to rise. He finally charges with a trident. Hanumān and Aṅgada knock him down, while Lakṣmaṇa shatters a spear hurled at him. The demon fights by changing forms and vanishing; when even the monkeys fear his apparent invincibility, Lakṣmaṇa resolves to end the sport. Remembering the Lord of Kosala, he releases a proud shaft into Meghanāda’s chest. At death the demon abandons deceit, cries ‘Where is Rāma’s younger brother? Where is Rāma?’ and yields his life; Aṅgada and Hanumān praise his mother as blessed.",
