      "meaning": "The immense fourfold demon army advances in many columns, with varied mounts, chariots, standards and banners. Herds of intoxicated elephants move like monsoon clouds driven by wind; seasoned champions skilled in illusion fill the wondrous host. Its march makes the elephants of the quarters stumble, agitates the sea, shakes mountains and veils the sun with dust. Drums, trumpets and shawms thunder like doomsday clouds, while warriors roar out their prowess. Rāvaṇa orders them to crush the crowds of bears and monkeys and boasts that he will kill the two princes. Hearing this, the monkeys charge invoking Raghubīra.",
