    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0080",
      "sequence": 935,
      "meaning": "Seeing Rāvaṇa in a chariot and Rāma on foot, Vibhīṣaṇa anxiously asks how the Lord can conquer so mighty a warrior without chariot or armour. Rāma describes the true chariot of victory: valour and patience are its wheels; truth and good conduct its firm banner; strength, discernment, self-restraint and care for others its horses, harnessed by forgiveness, compassion and equanimity; worship of God its wise driver; detachment its shield and contentment its sword; charity its axe, intellect its power and mature knowledge its hard bow; a pure, steady mind its quiver, tranquillity and discipline its arrows, and reverence for brahmins and teachers its impenetrable armour. Whoever possesses this dharma-made chariot has no unconquerable enemy and can defeat even the great foe of worldly existence. Vibhīṣaṇa joyfully recognizes the gracious teaching. Meanwhile Rāvaṇa challenges from one side and Aṅgada and Hanumān from the other, each combatant fighting on his lord’s honour.",
